  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Continuing Pileated Gibbon Conservation Education and Public Outreach in Cambodia through the Kouprey Express</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will accomplish the following objectives: (1) Continue building capacity and understanding of key environmental issues for 300 teachers, community educators, and community leaders in communities, schools and NGOs in target areas as well as all other provinces through training, staff development, monitoring and evaluation; (2) Bring a gibbon-focused education curriculum to an estimated 7,500 students at national schools and NGOs around the country and in the Cardamom Mountains; (3) Conduct an anticipated 20 field trips to Phnom Tamao Wildlife Rescue Center to complement classroom lessons and environmental education awareness outreach activities for students and community members from around the country; (4) Build environmental awareness and pride in Cambodias natural heritage among students and communities through interactive hands-on Community Night Shows, which complement our work in schools; (5) Continue collaboration with other conservation NGOs on capacity building to help facilitate their own environmental education teams as a means of ensuring our message continues; (6) Continue to conduct Wildlife ID and anti-smuggling training with new Customs and Excise officers from Phnom Penh and Siem Reap International Airports and other relevant agencies; and, (7) Raise community awareness among Cambodians on a nationwide level regarding the devastating effects of the illegal wildlife trade with a focus on gibbons, destruction of habitats, and other factors threatening Cambodias wildlife through large-scale signage and outreach activities in collaboration with others.</narrative>
  </description>
